=== SUMMARY 2026-08-16T13:06:15+10:00 ===
Output: docs/alpine-v2-research.md
Key finds:
1. CPU PLL bootstrap decode (al_hal_bootstrap.c): V2 field 0x5=1700(UNVR)..0xE=2700 max; V3 to 3000.
2. PLL divider maps (al_hal_pll_map.h) v1 for V2: entries to 3000/3200 MHz; al_pll_freq_set writes regs directly (CPU PLL drives cores/caches/GIC).
3. NO alpine cpufreq/DVFS/OPP driver anywhere; NO community overclock reports. Freq fixed at boot strap.
4. DDR HAL supports DDR4-800..3200; V2 DDR PLL strap 0x6=1200MHz(DDR4-2400); timings via CVOS agent + SPD@0x57.
5. No public datasheet/TRM; delroth-alpine_hal IS the register doc (dual GPL/commercial, (C)2015).
Leaders: Bootlin(Petazzoni,abandoned 2019), delroth(HAL+QNAP), bcyangkmluohmars/filefly(6.12 UNVR), fabianishere(UDM), mornepousse, riptidewave93, rickmark(security).
Corrections: AL-314=A15 Alpine V1 (not our part); UNVR=AL-324 A57; MikroTik RB1100AHx4=AL21400 A15 NOT same SoC.
